Falsifies `system_tests::user::confined_fuzzer_tests::a_confined_fuzzer_reaches_nothing_it_was_not_granted`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64 (the hunk is portable region code).

The planted escape this driver's own oracle must find (milestone 779 (fuzz the surface a confined
process can reach), part (b)): `MemoryRegion::RETYPE_OBJECT` carves its object page from the machine's
free list instead of the caller's region, so a confined process that retypes a rendezvous, a
notification or an address space holds, and can map, a page outside every grant. The kernel stays
healthy: no panic, no wrong register, nothing a crash oracle would see. The conductor's capability
oracle reads the fill's page against the granted extents and says
"slot N filled with Rendezvous(..) (rights ..) after syscall 2 words [.., 2, ..], which grants
nothing" (or the object-page twin, "an object outside every grant"), naming the seed and step.

Expected to fail: the first seed whose fuzzers draw a `RETYPE_OBJECT` on their region, which the
committed suite range reaches within seconds of boot. Replayed red on aarch64 on 2026-10-06 (UTC)
by the lane for milestone 779 at seed 0, step 0: "fuzzer 0 holds Rendezvous(3, 0), an object
outside every grant".

